  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "Bandhan Financial Services, the promoter of Bandhan Bank, plans to gradually reduce its stake in the bank to conform to RBI regulations requiring a shareholding of 26% by 2030. Chairman Chandra Shekhar Ghosh stated that there are no plans for a bulk offloading in one go, with recent share sales having occurred on the open market to lower holdings from 39.74% at the end of 2025 down to 37.54% by the end of June. Additionally, the promoter has proposed a stock split dividing each equity share of face value 10 INR into five shares of face value 2 INR each, which shareholders are set to review at the annual general meeting scheduled for September 22.",
 "ticker": "BANDHANBNK.NS",
